    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0834" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/410: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-23T16:00:00-06:00">December 23,
                            1932—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>116. Referring to my telegram No. 115, December 20, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >3</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d773-f1"/> German Legation at Guatemala
                    City has advised German Consul here that German merchant vessel near Honduras
                    has been ordered to call at Amapala to take off foreign women and children and
                    foreigners who wish to leave the island. Permission to do so granted by
                    President Mejía Colindres. Military authorities here endeavoring to obtain four
                    launches from Salvador and with small boats believe they can retake Amapala.
                    Understand that bombing port from air abandoned. Military authorities believe
                    Reina with 100 armed followers has left island and joined force of about 300
                    insurgents now north of Goascoran and being pursued by Nationalist troops.
                    Congress extended martial law 60 days and authorized President to effect loan
                    for $500,000. Government has already hypothecated all its income for next 6
                    weeks available for guarantees except for small loan.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Central American missions and Comsperon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
